1. Install Apache web server on your Linux system and verify the installation by accessing the default Apache welcome page from your browser using localhost.
=>apt-get install -y apache2
service apache2 start
Verification:
Bashcurl http://localhost/

2. Change the default Apache web server homepage by editing the index.html file in /var/www/html to display your name and favorite IPL team.
=>/var/www/html/index.html:
HTML<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head><title>My Homepage</title></head>
<body>
  <h1>Hello, I am Grok</h1>
  <p>My favorite IPL team is Royal Challengers Bengaluru (RCB)!</p>
</body>
</html>
Result: Accessing http://localhost/

3. Configure a custom virtual host in Apache for a new domain called myzomatoclone.local that serves files from /var/www/myzomatoclone and test it by updating your /etc/hosts file.
=>mkdir -p /var/www/myzomatoclone
echo '<h1>Welcome to My Zomato Clone</h1><p>Order food online!</p>' > /var/www/myzomatoclone/index.html
Virtual host config (/etc/apache2/sites-available/myzomatoclone.local.conf):
apache<VirtualHost *:80>
    ServerName myzomatoclone.local
    DocumentRoot /var/www/myzomatoclone
    <Directory /var/www/myzomatoclone>
        Options Indexes FollowSymLinks
        AllowOverride All
        Require all granted
    </Directory>
    ...
</VirtualHost>
Enabled site and updated hosts:
Basha2ensite myzomatoclone.local.conf
echo "127.0.0.1 myzomatoclone.local" >> /etc/hosts
service apache2 reload
Test:
Bashcurl http://myzomatoclone.local/
→ Welcome to My Zomato Clone

4. Enable and test the Apache mod_rewrite module by creating a rule that rewrites requests from /foodie to /index.html, then verify it works in your browser.<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Use the a2enmod command and edit the .htaccess file in your web root.</em>
=>a2enmod rewrite
.htaccess (in /var/www/html/ and the virtual host root):
apacheRewriteEngine On
RewriteRule ^foodie$ /index.html [L,R]
Test:
Bashcurl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code} %{redirect_url}\n" http://localhost/foodie
text302 http://localhost/index.html
